 "name": "ADM232AANZ",
 "kind": "interface",
 "manufacturer": "Analog Devices",
 "title": "ADM222, ADM232A, ADM242: 5 V dual RS-232 driver and receiver with 0.1 µF charge pump, 200 kB/s",
 "source": {
  "revision": "Rev. C",
  "pages": 11
 },
 "summary": "A family of RS-232 transceivers, each with two drivers and two receivers, running from one 5 V supply. An on-chip charge pump with four 0.1 µF capacitors doubles and inverts the supply to about ±10 V, so the drivers swing ±9 V typical into 3 kΩ and run at 200 kB/s or more. The ADM232A is the basic 16-pin part and a pin-for-pin replacement for MAX232A, AD232 and ADM232L; the 18-pin ADM222 adds a shutdown input that turns everything off, and the ADM242 adds both a shutdown that leaves the receivers alive and a receiver output enable. All are specified from -40 °C to +85 °C.",
 "key_figures": [
